## Summary

I found and fixed the bug in src/parse.py:4. The issue was an off-by-one error where the function was returning `parts[1]` instead of `parts[0]`. 

The bug caused:
- `first_word('hello world')` to incorrectly return 'world' instead of 'hello'
- `first_word('solo')` to crash with an IndexError

The fix was simple: change `return parts[1]` to `return parts[0]` to correctly return the first element of the split string.

Both tests now pass successfully.
